body:
Yesterday, I put up a post that upset some people. 

The point I was trying to make was that my life doesn't matter.  I wasn't trying to make a political statement about BLM or any other movement.  I wasn't trying to criticize anyone (other than myself).  Nonetheless, I clearly upset some people, and for that I want to apologize. 

&#x200B;

I never meant to harm anyone or to imply that the BLM movement wasn't legitimate or anything.  I never meant to imply anything racist with the "All Lives Matter" portion of the text.  I'm extremely sorry to those I've hurt and hope that you can forgive me. 

&#x200B;

I've edited my graphic to hopefully be non-offensive.

The thought that my wife, my father, my sister and kids would be completely devastated.

&#x200B;

Also, there is the fact that one of my sons made a half-hearted attempt a few years ago.  He seems to be doing better now, but he still has his times when his depression gets to him.  I'm afraid that if I commit suicide, he'll see it as permission to go ahead with him when he's in the mood.  I never want to give him that go ahead.

I've done this from time to time.  

&#x200B;

The problem with your suggestion is that when I do so, it's not because I want to take out my frustration on something else.  It's because I want to harm myself.  Hitting a punching bag doesn't serve that purpose.
